# Real Scryfall partial-candidate browser audit and repair

The requested real-run assertions pass against the repaired viewer. One material presentation defect was found and fixed: the original rejection reason's complete case hashes expanded a 390px mobile page to 498px. The decision panel also required readers to resolve those hashes manually to identify the failing cases.

The trigger is recorded decision `11bd1d52f3d2dd823d3e72194beb7bf735fcc6d8c1cb455cec33c1ab9e6f00cb`, sequence 863, in `scryfall-mana-20260907-03`, for candidate patch `0e87162bb9e09f10a87722015e9d7d6fbbc2fcea269392bec47486f729ba5017`. The offending element is `.decision-card.rejected > ul > li`: its content width was 447px within a 304px element. With wrapping, content and element both fit 304px and the page fits 390px. The complete reason text is unchanged; before/after measurements and exact text are retained in `ui-repair-evidence.json`.

The scoped viewer change adds wrapping in both rejection surfaces and “Recorded candidate gate violations” with links to Deranged Assistant, Millikin and their feedback evidence. Names and evidence are joined through this decision's exact frozen plan, candidate execution records and strong violated feedback, using globally visible events only through the decision sequence. The implementation does not parse the original reason or infer acceptance from an empty violation set. Case selection and feedback-inspector links were exercised on the actual run.

