The queue preserves all 57 candidate results: 16 satisfied, 2 violated and 39 inconclusive. An actual inconclusive case was inspected and remained inconclusive. The candidate stays visibly rejected beside satisfied case evidence, and the overall run remains running. Seeking to sequence 862 hides the decision; sequence 863 restores the rejection. No accepted Scryfall decision is shown. Source Oracle text and the independent implementation-review summary remain accessible, including the review's explicit statement that source review is separate from experiment acceptance and the Mill cases remain unfixed.

Validation: TypeScript checking, 29 focused unit tests, all 9 existing factory browser tests (including a regression with the exact real rejection reason), and the bounded real-run browser audit. Unit coverage excludes unrelated plan/candidate feedback, weak or malformed execution bindings, and later feedback that would rewrite this decision. Desktop and mobile evidence/decision views have no horizontal page overflow after the fix. No JavaScript or HTTP errors occurred in the completed real-run audit.

The original view was checked on the existing server at port 8030. The repaired production build was served only in the reviewer's reserved workspace on port 4198; browser API requests read the unchanged real run from 8030. No replay data, native source, decision or shared server files were altered. Root deployment of the repaired viewer remains a separate step.

